SUMMARY:Tracy Grammer
LOCATION:Parlor Room\, 32 Masonic St\, Northampton\, MA 01060
DESCRIPTION:Called "a musician and singer of dazzling versatility" (No Depr
 ession)\, Tracy Grammer is among contemporary folk music's most beloved ar
 tists. Renowned for her pure voice\, deft guitar and violin work\, and inc
 antatory storytelling\, Grammer has recorded and performed with Joan Baez 
 and Mary Chapin Carpenter\, headlined several of the nation's top folk fes
 tivals\, including Philadelphia Folk Festival and Falcon Ridge\, and enjoy
 ed 12 consecutive years as one of folk radio's 50 top-played artists\, bot
 h solo and with the late Dave Carter.\nhttps://theparlorroom.my.salesforce
 -sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SV500000Cdr8nMAB\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: 
 https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://theparlorroom.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SV50000
 0Cdr8nMAB
END:VEVENT
