SUMMARY:Laura Cantrell
LOCATION:Parlor Room\, 32 Masonic St\, Northampton\, MA 01060
DESCRIPTION:On July 17th\, Propeller Sound Recordings will rerelease countr
 y music artist Laura Cantrell’s Humming By The Flowered Vine\, originall
 y released in 2005 on Matador Records. The “Humming album\,” as it bec
 ame known to Cantrell fans\, is a pivotal work in Cantrell’s music caree
 r – her previous recordings Not The Tremblin’ Kind and When the Roses 
 Bloom Again had been released in the UK by Glasgow-based indie label Spit 
 and Polish/Shoeshine\; in the US\, they had been the first full-length\, s
 ingle artist releases on Brooklyn’s Diesel Only Records\, run by Cantrel
 l’s husband Jeremy Tepper\, and they’d established Cantrell as an Amer
 icana talent on the rise. “With my first two albums\, we’d had an inte
 nse five years – starting with Tremblin’ Kind’s release in January 2
 000\, from our first appearance at Celtic Connections in Glasgow that year
 \, we sprinted nonstop – touring all over the UK and Ireland\, earning t
 he support and friendship of BBC legends John Peel and Bob Harris\, openin
 g for Willie Nelson and Elvis Costello in the US\, playing every kind of g
 ig from local bars all the way to the Grand Ole Opry\, it was a terrific b
 lur of hard work and happy accidents\,” Cantrell recalls.\nhttps://thepa
 rlorroom.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SV500000CxsNFMAZ\nFrom 
 Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://theparlorroom.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/events/a0SV50000
 0CxsNFMAZ
END:VEVENT
